A timer's `@tick` body is lowered like any other imperative body.

`timer` is an ordinary component, so the inliner has already put this one in the
window before either target's override is reached. The two targets here reach
it by different routes, and each route had the same gap in a different place.

bubbletea keeps a primitive, which passTimerPrimitive takes out of the tree and
records on its owner. That owner is an `ir.Window`, and `walkWindow` in
internal/lower/walk.go -- the traversal passNoTernary, passIndexedIter,
passNoRef and NoDeclarative's id scan all ride on -- walked a window's vars,
funcs and body and not its timers. Nothing in source puts a timer there, so the
omission was invisible until the pass that creates one ran.

fyne's override is an `effect`, so the tick is a lambda handed to a host
scheduler -- and a lambda's body is an expression's insides, which walkPackage
hands over to nobody. passNoTernary reaches one through a case of its own and
passIndexedIter did not, so the ternary came out lowered and the loop beside it
kept the second variable Go rejects over a range func. lowerIndexedIter collects
the lambdas separately for that.

The ternary is the loud half: it reached the Go emitter intact and panicked the
build with "ir.Ternary reached Go codegen". The two-variable loop over a
`sngl:seq` range is the silent half -- a pull sequence hands out no ordinal, so
passIndexedIter counts one alongside, and without it Go got
`for i, x := range slices.Values(...)`, which is a compile error, and Kotlin got
an index bound to nothing.

The same body in an `@click` handler lowered correctly throughout, which is what
isolated the position rather than the constructs.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `for i, x := range` -- a pull sequence hands out no index; passIndexedIter counts one alongside
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `for i, x := range` -- the same claim reached through a lambda instead, since this platform schedules with an effect

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import time "sngl:time"
import seq "sngl:seq"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
    }
}

component ticker ui.node {
    var level = 0.0
    var rung = 0

    time.timer(interval=50ms, @tick {
        level = level >= 1 ? 0.0 : level + 0.01
        for var i, x = seq.count(3) {
            rung = rung + i * x
        }
    })

    ui.text(value="{level} {rung}")
}

ui.window #main(title="tick") {
    ticker()
}
